WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
A loss turns “good” into a number.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.589
Training needs a single scalar to minimize.

3
00:00:04.869 --> 00:00:12.997
The video uses the sum of squared errors over the dataset: L = sum over examples of (prediction minus target) squared.

4
00:00:13.277 --> 00:00:24.029
Its derivative with respect to a prediction is 2 (prediction minus target), so each example pushes its own prediction toward its target with a force proportional to the error.

5
00:00:24.309 --> 00:00:26.187
Big mistakes get big gradients.

6
00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:29.773
The choice of loss is a modeling decision, not a detail.

7
00:00:30.053 --> 00:00:37.648
Squared error is the natural loss for regression with Gaussian noise (minimizing it is maximum likelihood under that assumption).

8
00:00:37.928 --> 00:00:47.379
From the next lesson on, the series switches to negative log-likelihood (cross-entropy), the natural loss for predicting a category such as the next character.

9
00:00:47.659 --> 00:00:52.971
The training machinery doesn’t change at all: one scalar, one backward pass, one update.
